sub-LU unblock patch for DAFoam DALinearEqn.C (fiml-adjoint-conditioning-unblock)
=================================================================================
Target: DAFoam v5-series source tree as shipped in dafoam/opt-packages:latest
        (in-container repo root: /home/dafoamuser/dafoam/repos/dafoam).
Apply from the DAFoam repo root (the directory containing src/):
        git apply DALinearEqn_subpclu.patch
    or  patch -p1 < DALinearEqn_subpclu.patch

Regenerated 2026-08-07 per SUPERVISOR_FAMILY_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md finding B-2:
the previous committed diff carried absolute headers into a session-ephemeral
scratchpad and failed `git apply` outright. This version uses repo-relative
a/ b/ headers and passes `git apply --check` against the stock source extracted
from dafoam/opt-packages:latest (verified 2026-08-07).

Content provenance (verified hunk-by-hunk against the container):
  * The 19-line DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE=lu block is byte-identical to the change
    applied in the deployed image dafoam-subpclu:v1 (extracted and diffed
    against stock 2026-08-07). All recorded sub-LU results (W4 unblock,
    reason 2 / 667 iters, FD-verified gradient) were produced by that block.
  * NEXT-REBUILD DELTA (finding B-1): the `else if` warn block for
    unrecognized non-empty DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE values is NEW in this patch and
    is NOT in the currently built dafoam-subpclu:v1 library. It changes no
    numeric path (behavior stays stock ILU); it only adds an Info warning.
    Do not expect the warning line in logs from the v1 image; it lands at the
    next image rebuild. Until then, drivers must keep asserting the
    "DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE=lu: ASM sub-block PC set to complete LU" Info line
    before trusting any sub-LU result (FAMILY_SUPERVISION_GUIDELINES.md).

--- a/src/adjoint/DALinearEqn/DALinearEqn.C
+++ b/src/adjoint/DALinearEqn/DALinearEqn.C
@@ -264,6 +264,38 @@
 
         // The subpc type will almost always be ILU
         PCType localPCType = PCILU;
+        // fiml-adjoint-conditioning-unblock (2026-08-04): the ASM sub-block
+        // incomplete factorization hits an exact zero pivot on wall-resolved
+        // separated cases (CBFS 21k, NASA hump 51.6k): ILU returns
+        // KSPConvergedReason -9 DIVERGED_NANORINF at iteration 0 for some
+        // orderings and a flat -3 for others, while a complete LU with
+        // pivoting solves the same dumped system. PETSc factor shift
+        // MAT_SHIFT_NONZERO (below) does not catch it because the failure is
+        // factor growth, not a small pivot. Setting the env var
+        // DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE=lu switches the sub-block PC to complete LU.
+        // Off by default; no behavior change unless the env var is set.
+        const char* subPCTypeEnv = getenv("DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE");
+        if (subPCTypeEnv && strcmp(subPCTypeEnv, "lu") == 0)
+        {
+            localPCType = PCLU;
+            if (i == 0)
+            {
+                Info << "DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE=lu: ASM sub-block PC set to complete LU" << endl;
+            }
+        }
+        // B-1 hardening (2026-08-07, SUPERVISOR_FAMILY_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md):
+        // any OTHER non-empty value (LU, Lu, trailing space, superlu, ...) used
+        // to fall through SILENTLY to stock ILU -- a run believed patched could
+        // be stock with no in-log tell. Warn loudly; behavior still stock ILU.
+        else if (subPCTypeEnv && subPCTypeEnv[0] != '\0')
+        {
+            if (i == 0)
+            {
+                Info << "WARNING: DAFOAM_SUBPC_TYPE set to unrecognized value '"
+                     << subPCTypeEnv << "'; only 'lu' (exact, lowercase) is"
+                     << " recognized. ASM sub-block PC remains stock ILU." << endl;
+            }
+        }
         PCSetType(MLRsubpc, localPCType);
 
         // Set PC factor
